The function body itself has little room to improve, so this is a small micro-optimization; I have not measured it.

- **Hoisted loads:** the field-array pointer and the field count are read into locals once. The compiler can then keep them in registers instead of re-reading them through `mesg` on every iteration.
- **Wider loop counter:** the counter is a native `unsigned int` rather than `FIT_UINT16`, which avoids 16-bit wraparound handling. It only takes values below `numFields`, so the conversion back to `FIT_UINT16` gives the same index.
- **Behavior unchanged:** results and return values are identical to the original.

```cpp
const FIT_UINT16 Profile::GetFieldIndex(const FIT_UINT16 mesgNum, const FIT_UINT8 fieldNum)
{
    const MESG *mesg = GetMesg(mesgNum);

    if (mesg == NULL)
        return FIT_UINT16_INVALID;

    const FIELD *const fields = mesg->fields;
    const unsigned int n = mesg->numFields;

    for (unsigned int i = 0; i < n; i++)
    {
        if (fields[i].num == fieldNum)
            return (FIT_UINT16)i;
    }

    return FIT_UINT16_INVALID;
}
```